    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "Aniline ketone m36 moved later than predicted, especially at 2/1: 23.42/39.43 measured versus 7.43/22.48 predicted. Pyridyl ketone m66 in pure EA had a smaller but still completion-dominant underprediction, 5.58/21.09 versus 6.48/14.28.",
      "implication": "Connectivity matters beyond a ring-nitrogen versus aniline distinction, but the sign of the residual changes by graph. A blanket nitrogen offset is contraindicated."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "Hydroxyl response growth continued beyond the model's learned curve. m99 at 10/1 measured 38.99/58.03 versus 18.40/29.34 predicted. m120 measured 19.89/29.02 at 2/1 and 50.73/71.53 at 5/1 versus 11.63/21.60 and 18.63/38.05 predicted. m61 at 2/1 also exceeded prediction by 5.19/9.12 mL.",
      "implication": "Hydroxyl placement, neighboring ether or ester connectivity, and ratio response require molecule-specific interaction learning. The previous predicted m99 decline is rejected."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "m82 interpolation at 5/1 was accurate, and its measured 20/1 rise was learned reasonably. Related m94 at 20/1 still had residuals of -8.06/-14.57 mL.",
      "implication": "The beta-ketoester response transfers partially, but related-graph extrapolation remains imperfect, especially for completion."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "m194's broad 1/1 interval did not persist at half loading: the high-load record was 4.35/36.18, while the low-load 1/1 record was 4.26/10.34. The low-load 2/1 record was 5.93/14.73.",
      "implication": "The hypothesis of a loading-independent broad completion interval is substantially weakened. Loading or an associated condition interaction can affect completion, but these records do not establish a general loading law."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "The m173 5/1 smaller-plug experiment was close to prediction at 11.88/61.87 versus 13.94/62.89. Pure EA remained lower at 3.56/31.91, while the smaller-plug 1/1 record retained a late completion of 78.37.",
      "implication": "The unusual tail is localized near the weak-eluent 1/1 condition. A ratio-by-plug interaction remains plausible, but a universal plug correction is unsupported."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "observed measured evidence",
      "behavior": "The naphthyl-shape continuation failed for m124: 6.31/13.07 measured versus 19.30/19.54 predicted at 20/1. m40 also had a predicted onset that was too late, although its completion was close.",
      "implication": "The proposed cross-functionality naphthyl onset delay and interval compression should be weakened. Sparse-anchor shape extrapolation is unreliable in this region."
    },
    {
      "evidence_type": "model diagnostic",
      "behavior": "Loading sensitivity remains nearly absent in current predictions. At m92 2/1, the low-to-high-load predicted completion change is about 0.054 mL versus a measured change of 0.825 mL; at 10/1, the predicted change is about 0.058 versus a measured change of 3.479 mL.",
      "implication": "Condition features, especially loading amount and their interactions with eluent and graph structure, are weakly routed or weakly represented. More broad loading grids have low value until this bottleneck is addressed."
