    "Exact-input repeats are valuable only when they address reproducibility or omitted-condition variation. The conflicting m73 records demonstrate that local variation exists, but they do not estimate a global noise floor.",
    "Similarity, novelty, condition novelty, predicted retention, and quantile width are insufficient alone. Several high-signal candidates are continuation points in already-failed response regions, while lower-uncertainty candidates can still test competing explanations."
